    {
      "item_id": "S-001-US1",
      "level": "story",
      "parent_id": "E-001",
      "title": "Every change is built, tested and shipped safely",
      "description_md": "As the delivery team, we want each commit to the API and web repositories to be built, tested, scanned and deployed through one repeatable pipeline, so that Release 1 can be shipped on 1 March 2027 without manual, error-prone steps and a bad release can be undone quickly. **Why this priority**: Every other feature depends on a working pipeline, and the go-live date is firm (NFR-009). Without it nothing can reach staging or production. **Independent Test**: Push a trivial commit to the API repository and to the web repository. Confirm each pipeline runs every stage in order, a deliberately failing test or a seeded HIGH vulnerability stops the pipeline before deployment, and a deliberately failing health check triggers a rollback to the previous release. **Acceptance Scenarios**: 1. **Given** a commit to the API repository, **When** the pipeline runs, **Then** it builds, runs unit tests, runs contract tests against the published API contract, scans the image, deploys to staging, runs the smoke test (health, sign-in with a test code, book and cancel against sandbox providers) and only then replaces production one replica at a time behind the health check. 2. **Given** a failing unit test, a contract test that no longer matches the API contract, or a HIGH image-scan finding, **When** the pipeline runs, **Then** the pipeline stops and nothing is deployed to staging or production. 3. **Given** a commit to the web repository, **When** the pipeline runs, **Then** the web app is built and published separately from the API and the previous published build is kept. 4. **Given** a new release in production, **When** the health check fails, or server errors exceed 2% for 5 minutes, or reminder lag exceeds 15 minutes, **Then** the team can roll back by redeploying the previous API image and the previous web build, and the rollback steps are documented and rehearsed once in staging. 5. **Given** a database change in a release, **When** the pipeline deploys it, **Then** the change only adds or relaxes structures (expand) and stays compatible with the previous release; removals happen in a later release (contract). ---",
      "type": "feature",
      "speckit_phase": "user_story",
      "priority": "P1",
      "moscow": "must",
      "user_story": {
        "as_a": "member of the delivery team",
        "i_want": "each commit to the API and web repositories built, tested, scanned and deployed through one repeatable pipeline with a rehearsed rollback",
        "so_that": "Release 1 can ship on 1 March 2027 without manual, error-prone steps and a bad release can be undone quickly"
      },
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "ac_id": "AC-S-001-US1-1",
